# coding-standards.mdc — Interview Architect

```yaml
codingStandards:
  languages:
    TypeScript:
      version: "^5.8.3"
      rules:
        - Use strict TypeScript with noUncheckedIndexedAccess, isolatedModules, and verbatimModuleSyntax.
        - Use type-only imports when importing only types.
        - Preserve explicit interfaces at shared API and repository boundaries.
    SQL:
      rules:
        - Add forward-only, append-only D1 migrations under infra/migrations.
        - Use parameterized statements through the repository layer.
    CSS:
      rules:
        - Extend existing visual tokens and responsive breakpoints before adding isolated styles.
        - Keep keyboard focus, contrast, responsive behavior, and reduced-motion preferences intentional.

  frameworks:
    React:
      rules:
        - Use function components and hooks.
        - Keep route-level code lazy-loaded and split large feature pages into focused components/hooks when adding substantial behavior.
        - Preserve the URL as the source of truth for question-bank filter state.
    Hono:
      rules:
        - Validate request bodies and parameters with Zod strict schemas.
        - Keep HTTP orchestration in app.ts and persistence in the repository interface.
    CloudflareWorkers:
      rules:
        - Keep Worker bindings typed and same-origin API paths compatible with static asset deployment.

  testing:
    framework: Vitest and Playwright
    runner: npm workspaces; vitest run for package/API tests and playwright test for browser journeys
    location: apps/api/test, packages/content/test, packages/domain/test, tests/e2e
    requirements:
      - New domain and repository behavior requires focused Vitest coverage.
      - New API behavior requires Hono/API integration coverage, including auth and malformed-input cases when relevant.
      - New learner workflows require Playwright end-to-end coverage of their success path and critical failure/retry path.
      - Run content validation when content schema or records change.
      - Preserve privacy-deletion, anonymous-session, and origin-check tests for changes touching learner state.
    coverage:
      tool: Vitest coverage is not configured; CI enforces scenario coverage through test suites.
      threshold: null

  naming:
    commits: conventional
    packages: match existing workspace layout and @interview-architect namespace

  review:
    blockingSeverities: [BLOCKER]
    strictReview: false
    dimensions:
      - product correctness
      - architecture
      - privacy and security
      - accessibility
      - performance
      - reliability
      - maintainability
      - entropy
    securityChecks:
      - no secrets in code or config commits
      - validate API input and use parameterized D1 statements
      - protect write routes with existing trusted-origin rules
      - do not render untrusted raw HTML or unsanitized diagram markup
      - do not edit .cursor kit files outside project-context

  entropy:
    enabled: true
    policy: remove-on-touch
    onChange:
      - remove unused symbols and commented-out code
      - delete superseded components, hooks, tests, and storage keys when replacing behavior
      - remove orphaned config and stale documentation statements in touched areas
    blockReview:
      - new commented-out code without tracked reason
      - parallel superseded implementation left in diff
      - duplicated persistence behavior outside the repository boundary
    reference: .cursor/sdlc-system/workflow/entropy-management.md

  documentation:
    sdlcArtifacts: docs/sdlc/{workflowId}/
    projectGuide: README.md
    stackRules: []
```
